{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgF8Xn7BYs5pimKSR43ga","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"prompt\": \"A square abstract painting that fills the entire canvas edge to edge, with no frame, wall, room, or gallery setting. Purely nonrepresentational: no recognizable objects, figures, faces, bodies, scenes, landscapes, horizons, machines, diagrams, symbols, icons, letters, numbers, or text. Composition: a dense, dark indigo-black field at the lower left, pressed against a cluster of hot vermilion and ochre strokes that surge upward and diagonally toward the upper right, creating strong spatial tension. Between them, a band of cool, pale grey-green scraped thin with a palette knife, suggesting a held breath or a decision not yet made. Brushwork alternates between loaded, fast, slashing gestures with visible drips and slow, dry-brush drags that leave the ground showing through. Layering: several translucent glazes build depth, with earlier underlayers of cobalt and burnt sienna bleeding through the surface. Texture ranges from thick impasto ridges catching light to smooth, almost wet-looking patches. Rhythm comes from repeated short vertical marks in the upper third that pulse like a rapid sequence, contrasted with a single long, unbroken curve sweeping across the middle. Leave one area of raw, unpainted canvas near the center right as deliberate empty space, offering a pause. High contrast between the saturated warm mass and the restrained cool passages; no single focal point, and the energy reads as pressure, restraint, and a search for clarity. Painterly, expressive, gallery-quality detail, rendered as a flat, full-bleed square image.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":545,"cache_read_input_tokens":15150,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":545},"output_